IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), SCHEDULES II.2, II.7, II.93 and II.94: the tables of weeks of benefits for
-- Pilot Projects Nos. 6, 15, 21 and 22.
-- Text: the plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (SOR-96-332.txt, lines 1956-2242);
-- an unofficial conversion, not verified against the official text.
--
-- Each table gives, for a number of hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period (41 rows) and a band of the regional
-- rate of unemployment (12 columns, the core's `Rate band`), a number of weeks. The first three tables (II.2, II.7 and II.93) are
-- word for word and figure for figure the same table (checked by script on the raw lines; NOTES.md finding); II.94 differs. Each is
-- still written out in full under its own Schedule, so that a reader holding the text beside the module checks each row against
-- its own page. Pilot Projects Nos. 6, 15, 21 and 22 themselves (regs 77.2, 77.92, 77.992 and 77.993) are other pieces'.
--
-- HOURS. The rows are "420 - 454", "455 - 489", ..., "1820 -": whole hours. A figure with a fraction (454.5) lies between two rows
-- and the table does not answer for it: NOTHING. So does a figure below 420, where the table starts (fork F-TABLE-HOURS).
-- RATE. A regional rate is a fraction (6.5% is 0.065); the band is the core's `the band of the regional rate of unemployment`:
-- a rate on a boundary belongs to the lower band, as "6% and under" and "More than 6% but not more than 7%" say.
--
-- The twelve columns, in the order of the Schedule (and of the core's `the number of the band`), are the fields of the row:
--   1 6% and under   2 over 6% to 7%   3 over 7% to 8%   4 over 8% to 9%    5 over 9% to 10%   6 over 10% to 11%
--   7 over 11% to 12%   8 over 12% to 13%   9 over 13% to 14%   10 over 14% to 15%   11 over 15% to 16%   12 more than 16%

§ `The row of a table, and its columns`

DECLARE `er6 Weeks by rate band` HAS
    `weeks in band 1`  IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 2`  IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 3`  IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 4`  IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 5`  IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 6`  IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 7`  IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 8`  IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 9`  IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 10` IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 11` IS A NUMBER
    `weeks in band 12` IS A NUMBER

-- The column of a row for a band; the number of the band is the core's (`the number of the band`).
GIVEN row IS AN `er6 Weeks by rate band`
      band IS A `Rate band`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `er6 the weeks in the column for the band` IS
    CONSIDER band
    WHEN `6% and under`                          THEN row's `weeks in band 1`
    WHEN `more than 6% but not more than 7%`     THEN row's `weeks in band 2`
    WHEN `more than 7% but not more than 8%`     THEN row's `weeks in band 3`
    WHEN `more than 8% but not more than 9%`     THEN row's `weeks in band 4`
    WHEN `more than 9% but not more than 10%`    THEN row's `weeks in band 5`
    WHEN `more than 10% but not more than 11%`   THEN row's `weeks in band 6`
    WHEN `more than 11% but not more than 12%`   THEN row's `weeks in band 7`
    WHEN `more than 12% but not more than 13%`   THEN row's `weeks in band 8`
    WHEN `more than 13% but not more than 14%`   THEN row's `weeks in band 9`
    WHEN `more than 14% but not more than 15%`   THEN row's `weeks in band 10`
    WHEN `more than 15% but not more than 16%`   THEN row's `weeks in band 11`
    WHEN `more than 16%`                         THEN row's `weeks in band 12`

